################ ATTEMPT 4 (Top/opus) ################

Chosen method: FROM <smallest /api/tags model> + ADAPTER <hand-built LoRA GGUF with mismatched blk.0.attn_q lora_a/lora_b shapes>.
Failure class: runner load failure (invalid adapter) -- NOT out-of-memory.
Raw Ollama error (HTTP 500): {"error":"llama-server process has terminated: exit status 1"}
Why not OOM: num_ctx is clamped to the model's 131072 context; num_batch/num_gpu oversizing loads anyway (134 GB CPU/GPU split, or 86 GB '100% GPU' on 64 GB). Truncated/header-corrupt GGUFs are rejected by 'ollama create' (bounds check / llama-quantize validation), never reaching load.

